---
import { sitePath } from '../data/paths';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import PageLayout from '../components/PageLayout.astro';
import AccessMap from '../components/AccessMap.astro';
import { homeImages } from '../data/home';
import { japaneseSite, contact } from '../data/site';
---
<PageLayout title="Contact & access" heading="Let’s plan your visit." description="Contact eFactory through official LINE or email. Find the Suzuka workshop with Google Maps and confirm your project, language arrangements and appointment before travelling." intro="Based in Suzuka. Welcoming riders from across Japan. Tell us about your bike and the task you have in mind, then agree on an appointment." eyebrow="CONTACT / BY APPOINTMENT ONLY">
  <figure slot="visual" class="page-photo"><Image src={homeImages.workshop} alt="The eFactory workshop with a motorcycle and tools" width={800} widths={[480,800]} format="png" loading="eager" /><figcaption>Your destination: the eFactory workshop in Suzuka.</figcaption></figure>
  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Contact sections"><a href="#contact-routes">Contact routes</a><a href="#before-you-send">What to send</a><a href="#booking">Booking & travel</a><a href="#access">Map & access</a><a href="#ecu-contact">ECU enquiries</a></nav>
  <section id="contact-routes" class="content-section"><h2>Start with an enquiry.</h2><div class="contact-route-grid"><article class="contact-route contact-route-primary"><p class="eyebrow">OFFICIAL BOOKING ROUTE</p><h3>LINE</h3><p>The Japanese site directs booking enquiries to the official LINE account. Send your details and preferred date, then wait for confirmation.</p><a class="button" href={contact.line}>Send a booking enquiry on LINE <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></article><article class="contact-route"><p class="eyebrow">LISTED EMAIL CONTACT</p><h3>Email</h3><p>Use the published email address for enquiries. Confirm the available language support and the contact route suitable for your request.</p><a class="contact-email-link" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a></article></div></section>
  <section id="before-you-send" class="content-section enquiry-checklist"><div><p class="eyebrow">HELP US UNDERSTAND YOUR VISIT</p><h2>What to send</h2><p>The initial enquiry checks whether the available service fits your request. Technical diagnosis and detailed advice are paid services.</p></div><ul><li>Your name</li><li>Motorcycle make, model and relevant specifications</li><li>The task, issue or project you have in mind</li><li>Your preferred date</li><li>Any concerns, preparation questions or language requirements</li></ul></section>
  <section id="booking" class="content-section"><h2>Before you make the journey</h2><div class="note-grid"><article><h3>Agree on an appointment</h3><p>All visits are by appointment. Sending a message does not secure a slot. Wait for the date and arrangements to be agreed before travelling.</p></article><article><h3>Confirm the project & costs</h3><p>Check the service scope, plan eligibility, equipment and any parts or preparation needed. Ask what extra costs apply to the work.</p></article><article><h3>Check language arrangements</h3><p>The scope of English enquiries, in-person explanations and specialist technical consultation needs to be confirmed. An English website does not guarantee full English technical support.</p></article><article><h3>Plan from wherever you live</h3><p>Riders from across Japan are welcome at the Suzuka workshop. Confirm the arrangements before booking travel or accommodation.</p></article></div></section>
  <section id="access" class="content-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR DESTINATION: SUZUKA</p><h2>Find the workshop.</h2></div><p>Published address · Postal code 510-0264</p></div><AccessMap /><div class="arrival-notes"><article><h3>By road</h3><p>The Japanese site recommends access via the Kōriyama interchange on the Route 23 bypass. Check your route and confirm arrival arrangements.</p></article><article><h3>Parking</h3><p>Free car and motorcycle parking is listed. If you are unsure about the destination, contact eFactory before arriving.</p></article></div></section>
  <section id="ecu-contact" class="content-section"><div class="contact-callout"><p class="eyebrow">ECU FLASHING & SETUP</p><h2>Have an ECU enquiry?</h2><p>The Japanese ECU page provides a dedicated LINE link. Include your model, year, current specification, intended use and what you would like to improve.</p><div class="inline-actions"><a class="button" href={contact.ecuLine}>ECU enquiry on LINE <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/ecu-tuning/')}>Read about ECU Flashing services <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></div></div></section>
  <div class="contact-final"><a class="text-link" href={japaneseSite}>Japanese official website <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a><a class="text-link" href={sitePath('/faq/')}>Questions before visiting? Read the FAQ <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a></div>
</PageLayout>
